silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_concrete_anchor%23d_mittens_category
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "YonedaLemmaStatementConcreteAnchorAddlBaseTopic" ;
    rdfs:label "YonedaLemmaStatementConcreteAnchorAddlCircuitCorner" ;
    rdfs:label "YonedaLemmaStatementConcreteAnchorAddlDunbarLayer" ;
    rdfs:label "YonedaLemmaStatementConcreteAnchorAddlPaperKind" ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.00_whitepaper.chapters.07_yoneda_profile_drill.sections.02_yoneda_lemma_statement.concrete_anchor#d_mittens_category" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "base_topic:category theory" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "circuit_corner:2" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "dunbar_layer:0" ;
    silm:hasAdditionalAttribute "paper_kind:urn:silmaril:entity#papers.00_whitepaper" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The D_Mittens_Category is D_Mittens_Category: the locally small category used as the instantiation of C in the Yoneda lemma statement; objects = twelve source nodes + MittensColimitApex; morphisms = the twelve typed legs plus identity arrows and compositions." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_concrete_anchor
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "YonedaLemmaStatementConcreteAnchorExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'YonedaLemmaStatementConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, D_Mittens_Category: the locally small category used as the instantiation of C in the Yoneda lemma statement; objects = twelve source nodes + MittensColimitApex; morphisms = the twelve typed legs plus identity arrows and compositions; also, MittensColimitApex: the concrete instantiation of the object A in the Yoneda lemma; the colimit of D_Mittens; Mittens-the-individual-cat assembled from all twelve legs; also, ClinicalLabelPresheaf: the concrete instantiation of the presheaf F; assigns to each D_Mittens source node X the set of clinical labels for X stored in VetRecord_77 or associated clinic systems." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_decomposition_step__step_c__a__hom_c___a__f__nat______iso__evaluation_at_1_a
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "C is a locally small category (one whose hom-sets are sets, not proper classes). A is any object of C. Hom_C(-, A) is the representable presheaf: it sends each object B to the set of arrows from B to A, and each morphism f : B -> B' to the precomposition map -o f. F is any presheaf, i.e. a contravariant functor F : C^op -> Set. Nat(-, -) names the set of natural transformations between two functors. iso means there is a bijection (natural in A and F). The evaluation map sends a natural transformation alpha : Hom(-, A) -> F to its component at A applied to the identity arrow 1_A : A -> A." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_bijection_phialpha_%3D_alpha_a1_a%3B_inverse_psix_bf_%3D_ffx
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Yoneda bijection phi : Nat(Hom(-, A), F) -> F(A) sends a natural transformation alpha to its component at A applied to the identity, i.e. phi(alpha) = alpha_A(1_A) which lives in F(A). Its inverse psi : F(A) -> Nat(Hom(-, A), F) is defined by (psi(x))_B(f) = F(f)(x) for any f : B -> A in C; this assigns to each arrow f the F-image of x along F(f). The bijection is natural: for any morphism g : A -> A' the naturality square commutes." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_lemma__presheaf_category__naturality
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Joy of Cats Section 6.20 (Yoneda embedding is full and faithful) is the categorical base topic; the Yoneda lemma itself is also stated in Joy of Cats Section 6.18 (representable functors). Mac Lane \"Categories for the Working Mathematician\" Chapter III Section 2 calls it the most important result in category theory; Awodey \"Category Theory\" Section 8.3; Riehl \"Category Theory in Context\" Section 2.2. The lemma says objects are determined up to isomorphism by their representable presheaves; this is the formal underpinning of the sous-position observation discipline." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_decomposition_step__step_mittens_specific_yoneda_iso_instance
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Anchor: C = D_Mittens, A = Mittens (colimit apex of D_Mittens), F = ClinicalLabelPresheaf assigning to each D_Mittens source X the set of clinical labels (visit date, weight, microchip, species, audit trail, ...) attached to that source. The Yoneda iso says that a natural transformation tau from Hom(-, Mittens) into ClinicalLabelPresheaf is the same data as one clinical label at Mittens, namely the value tau_Mittens(1_Mittens)." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_decomposition_step__step_spine_inheritance_of_yoneda_iso_across_all_41_downstream_papers
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Yoneda spine traversal: paper-00 (this paper) supplies the Yoneda iso once; every downstream encyclopedia paper inherits a Mittens-Yoneda profile. Paper-02 (taxonomy) reads Hom(FelisCatusTSN183798, Mittens); paper-05 (measurement) reads Hom(BodyMassMeas_99, Mittens); paper-15 (KG growth) reads Hom(SHACLPassReport_77, Mittens); paper-19 (mereology) reads Hom(VetRecord_77, Mittens) and folds it into a mereology term; paper-25 (sheaf gluing) reads the entire Yoneda profile and glues it under sheaf-descent. No downstream paper redefines the Yoneda iso; each Yoneda-reads from the spine." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_02_yoneda_lemma_statement_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_lemma_statement_recap
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Nat(Hom(-, A), F) is in natural bijection with F(A) via evaluation at the identity 1_A. For Mittens this says: knowing the whole incoming Yoneda profile of Mittens, plus a presheaf F over D_Mittens, is the same as knowing the value of F at Mittens. This is the categorical guarantee that the sous observation discipline (read the apex through its arrows) is complete." .

