    silm:hasLongDescription "The TartuClinicIntakeForm is TartuClinicIntakeForm: the DICOM/HL7 intake form submitted for Mittens's May 2026 annual exam at the Tartu Animal Clinic; the raw source packet before any gate. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'SourcePacket', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_03_olog_node_arrow_law_concrete_anchor
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "OlogNodeArrowLawConcreteAnchorExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'OlogNodeArrowLawConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, TartuClinicIntakeForm: the DICOM/HL7 intake form submitted for Mittens's May 2026 annual exam at the Tartu Animal Clinic; the raw source packet before any gate; also, VetRecord_77: the ingested encyclopedia entry for Mittens's 2026-05-18 vet visit; output of the ingest gate; also, MittensSpeciesNode: VetRecord_77 with the species type DomesticCat / Felis catus / TSN 183798 assigned; output of the type gate." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_03_olog_node_arrow_law_decomposition_step__step_node_or_arrow_gate
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Node-or-Arrow gate is the admissibility test: every element in the local olog must be declared as either a node (typed object) or an arrow (typed morphism) before it can carry authority." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_03_olog_node_arrow_law_decomposition_step__step_publish_%3D_render_circ_validate_circ_type_circ_ingest_factori
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "circ is categorical composition in order: ingest first, then type, then validate, then render. The composition is the publish operation. Changing the order or skipping a gate changes the morphism." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_03_olog_node_arrow_law_decomposition_step__step_factorization_structure_joc_%C2%A715
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The factorization structure (JoC §15): a class of monomorphisms (source-truthful arrows) and a class of epimorphisms (surjective-type arrows) factor every morphism in a canonical way. The publish factorization is the categorical factorization for the olog's publish morphism." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_03_olog_node_arrow_law_decomposition_step__step_forbidden_shortcut
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The forbidden shortcut is TartuClinicIntakeForm -> VetCarePlanPDF_77 drawn as a direct dashed arrow, bypassing the ingest, type, validate, render gates." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_03_olog_node_arrow_law_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_inheritance_of_gate_law
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda naturality, the four-gate publish law is inherited by every downstream encyclopedia paper: when paper 24 (SHACL validation) claims a validation receipt, it must produce a receipt that is the output of a type gate (not a raw intake form). The gate law transports via the spine inheritance arrow." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_03_olog_node_arrow_law_decomposition_step__step_node_or_arrow_gate_recap
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Every olog element is a node or an arrow; publish factors as render circ validate circ type circ ingest; the forbidden shortcut TartuClinicIntakeForm -> VetCarePlanPDF_77 is blocked unless it is the four-gate composite; downstream papers inherit the gate law via Yoneda naturality." .

