    silm:hasExample "In 'UnitAndMultiplicationYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, In 'Unit and Multiplication', the monad_unit_arrow eta: VetRecord_77 -> T_Sigma(VetRecord_77) is the unit injection; monic because VetRecord_77 maps to a unique element of T_Sigma(VetRecord_77) (the single-leaf tree); different generators have different single-leaf trees.; also, In 'Unit and Multiplication', the monad_multiplication_arrow mu: T_Sigma(T_Sigma(VetRecord_77)) -> T_Sigma(VetRecord_77) flattens nested trees; not monic because different nested trees can flatten to the same tree (if the inner trees have the same leaves)." .

