silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_06_yoneda_for_mittens_concrete_anchor
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "YonedaForMittensConcreteAnchorExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'YonedaForMittensConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, D_Mittens_Category: the diagram category D_Mittens over which the Yoneda lemma is applied; its objects are the twelve typed source nodes (VetRecord_77, MicrochipID_44, BodyMassQuality, WeightMeas_3450g, Value_3450, Unit_grams, PetRole, SleepProcess_7h, SHACLPassReport_77, AuditTrail_77, DomesticCat, FelisCatusTSN183798); its apex is MittensColimitApex; also, MittensColimitApex: the colimit apex — the assembled individual Mittens; the object whose representable functor Hom(-,MittensColimitApex) is the Yoneda subject; also, ClinicalLabelPresheaf: the concrete presheaf that assigns to each D_Mittens source object X the set of clinical labels recorded against X in VetRecord_77; used as the concrete F in the Yoneda bijection Nat(Hom(-,Mittens), F) iso F(Mittens)." .

