silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_concrete_anchor__clinicallabelpresheaf
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00001069 ;
    rdfs:label "ClinicalLabelPresheaf: the contravariant functor D_Mittens^{op} -> Set that assigns to each typed source object X the set of clinical labels recorded against X in VetRecord_77 at the Tartu Animal Clinic on 2026-05-18; e.g. ClinicalLabelPresheaf(WeightMeas_3450g) = {hyperthyroidism_risk_normal, body_condition_score_5_of_9}; ClinicalLabelPresheaf(MicrochipID_44) = {chip_verified, chip_position_dorsal_neck_canonical}; the concrete F whose density-colimit decomposition the section demonstrates." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00001069 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_concrete_anchor__clinicalreadingcensus
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00000958 ;
    rdfs:label "ClinicalReadingCensus: the category of elements of ClinicalLabelPresheaf — its objects are pairs (X, x) where X is a D_Mittens source object and x is one of the clinical labels in ClinicalLabelPresheaf(X); e.g. (WeightMeas_3450g, hyperthyroidism_risk_normal) is one object, (MicrochipID_44, chip_verified) is another; arrows are restriction morphisms in D_Mittens that respect the presheaf action. The index category over which the density colimit is taken." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00000958 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_concrete_anchor__typedlegrepresentable
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00001069 ;
    rdfs:label "TypedLegRepresentable: the family of representables {Hom(-, VetRecord_77), Hom(-, MicrochipID_44), Hom(-, BodyMassQuality), Hom(-, WeightMeas_3450g), Hom(-, Value_3450), Hom(-, Unit_grams), Hom(-, PetRole), Hom(-, SleepProcess_7h), Hom(-, SHACLPassReport_77), Hom(-, AuditTrail_77), Hom(-, DomesticCat), Hom(-, FelisCatusTSN183798)}; one per typed leg of D_Mittens; each is the Yoneda profile of one source object, sent into ClinicalLabelPresheaf along the canonical natural transformation tau_X(x): Hom(-, X) -> ClinicalLabelPresheaf for each label x." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00001069 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_concrete_anchor__reconstructedclinicalpresheaf
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00001069 ;
    rdfs:label "ReconstructedClinicalPresheaf: the colimit (in the presheaf category [D_Mittens^{op}, Set]) of all twelve typed-leg representables, glued along the restriction arrows of ClinicalReadingCensus; the density theorem says this colimit is naturally isomorphic to ClinicalLabelPresheaf itself. Concretely: every clinical label recorded about Mittens at the Tartu clinic is recovered as one of the twelve typed-leg contributions, glued by the restriction morphisms." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00001069 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_concrete_anchor__yonedainjection
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00000686 ;
    rdfs:label "YonedaInjection: for each (X, x) in ClinicalReadingCensus, the natural transformation tau_{(X,x)}: Hom(-, X) -> ClinicalLabelPresheaf determined by the Yoneda lemma to send id_X to x; concretely, tau_{(WeightMeas_3450g, hyperthyroidism_risk_normal)} sends id_{WeightMeas_3450g} to the hyperthyroidism-risk-normal label, and propagates by naturality to every arrow ending at WeightMeas_3450g." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00000686 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_concrete_anchor__d_mittens_category
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00000958 ;
    rdfs:label "D_Mittens_Category: the locally small category indexing the Mittens source diagram; its twelve objects are the typed source nodes (VetRecord_77, MicrochipID_44, BodyMassQuality, WeightMeas_3450g, Value_3450, Unit_grams, PetRole, SleepProcess_7h, SHACLPassReport_77, AuditTrail_77, DomesticCat, FelisCatusTSN183798); its morphisms include the restriction arrows (e.g. WeightMeas_3450g -> BodyMassQuality), the identity arrows, and their composites. The density theorem ranges over the presheaf category [D_Mittens^{op}, Set]." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00000958 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_decomposition_step__step_colim_x__x_in_eltsf_hom___x
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "colim is the name of the colimit operation; (X, x) names a pair where X is a typed source node in D_Mittens (e.g. WeightMeas_3450g) and x is a label assigned to X (e.g. hyperthyroidism_risk_normal); Elts(F) names the category whose objects are all such pairs; Hom(-, X) names the representable functor at X (the functor sending each source Y to the set of arrows Y -> X)." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_decomposition_step__step_gluing_along_restriction_arrows
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gluing means: when one pair (X, x) maps into another pair (Y, y) along a morphism f: X -> Y of D_Mittens (such that the F-restriction of y along f equals x), the colimit identifies the Hom(-, X) contribution with its image in Hom(-, Y). The colimit operation glues the twelve typed-leg representables along the restriction morphisms between source objects." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_density_theorem
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Density theorem: every presheaf F over a small category D is canonically isomorphic to the colimit of its representable cover indexed by the category of elements Elts(F). Mac Lane, Categories for the Working Mathematician, Chapter III §7. Awodey, Category Theory, §8.4. The theorem licenses the colimit reconstruction of any presheaf from representables." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_decomposition_step__step_clinicallabelpresheaf_reconstruction
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The reconstruction proceeds leg by leg: ClinicalLabelPresheaf(WeightMeas_3450g) = {hyperthyroidism_risk_normal, body_condition_score_5_of_9} comes from the (WeightMeas_3450g, _) injections; ClinicalLabelPresheaf(MicrochipID_44) = {chip_verified, chip_position_dorsal_neck_canonical} comes from the (MicrochipID_44, _) injections; ClinicalLabelPresheaf(DomesticCat) = {mammalian_vital_signs_baseline_applicable, feline_specific_drug_dosing_required} from the (DomesticCat, _) injections; the colimit glues these compatibly. Every clinical label about Mittens is reachable through exactly one such gluing path." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_density_traversal
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By the Yoneda lemma (which we proved in chapter 07 §02): natural transformations Hom(-, X) -> F are in bijection with elements of F(X). The density theorem assembles these bijections across all (X, x): each pair contributes one natural transformation from a representable into F, and the cocone of all these natural transformations IS the colimit cocone exhibiting F as their colimit. The Yoneda traversal at the apex MittensColimitApex inherits to downstream papers: paper 18 (Presheaf Semantics) reads ClinicalLabelPresheaf via its density decomposition." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_07_density_argument_decomposition_step__step_density_argument_recap
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ClinicalLabelPresheaf over D_Mittens equals the colimit of the twelve typed-leg representables glued along restriction morphisms — every clinical fact about Mittens is reachable as a colimit-image of a (source-leg, label) pair, and downstream papers inherit this density decomposition via Yoneda naturality." .

