silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_concrete_anchor__careplaninheritancefunctor
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00001069 ;
    rdfs:label "CareplanInheritanceFunctor: the covariant functor D_Mittens -> Set that assigns to each typed-source object X the set of care-plan obligations that propagate FROM X downstream to VetCarePlan_77 and GroomingLog_42. For example, CareplanInheritanceFunctor(DomesticCat) = {annual_dental_exam_recommended, rabies_boost_q3yr_recommended}; CareplanInheritanceFunctor(FelisCatusTSN183798) = {feline_specific_vaccine_panel_required}. The concrete F^{co} whose co-Yoneda decomposition the section demonstrates." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00001069 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_concrete_anchor__mittensoutprofile
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00001069 ;
    rdfs:label "MittensOutProfile: the covariant representable Hom(MittensColimitApex, -); for each downstream object Y, it gives the set of arrows MittensColimitApex -> Y. Concrete elements: the arrow MittensColimitApex -> VetCarePlan_77 (the unique colimit mediator into the care plan competing cocone), MittensColimitApex -> GroomingLog_42 (the analogous mediator into the grooming log), MittensColimitApex -> ClinicReportSummary_2026Q2 (the arrow into the quarterly clinic report). The out-profile bundles all such arrows." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00001069 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_concrete_anchor__mittenscolimitapex
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00000562 ;
    rdfs:label "MittensColimitApex: the colimit-of-D_Mittens object; Mittens-the-individual-cat at the Tartu Animal Clinic on 2026-05-18, microchip 44B2F9, TSN 183798, 3450g, identified by VetRecord_77. The object whose covariant out-profile the section reads via co-Yoneda." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00000562 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_concrete_anchor__coyonedanaturaltransformationset
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00000686 ;
    rdfs:label "CoYonedaNaturalTransformationSet: the set of natural transformations from MittensOutProfile into CareplanInheritanceFunctor; the co-Yoneda lemma says this set is in bijection with CareplanInheritanceFunctor(MittensColimitApex) = the set of care-plan obligations attached at Mittens. Elements: the natural transformation tau^co_{care_obligation_x} sending id_{MittensColimitApex} to care_obligation_x." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00000686 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_concrete_anchor__mittenscareplanobligations
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00000853 ;
    rdfs:label "MittensCarePlanObligations: the concrete set CareplanInheritanceFunctor(MittensColimitApex) = {annual_dental_exam_recommended, rabies_boost_q3yr_recommended, feline_specific_vaccine_panel_required, weight_monitoring_q6mo_recommended}; the recovery target of the co-Yoneda bijection at Mittens; what is known about Mittens via the OUT-profile." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00000853 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_concrete_anchor__competingcoconeanchors
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    a cco:ont00000958 ;
    rdfs:label "CompetingCoconeAnchors: the family of objects {VetCarePlan_77, GroomingLog_42, ClinicReportSummary_2026Q2, BillingInvoice_2026_05_18} into which MittensColimitApex maps; each is a separate cocone over D_Mittens, and each receives a unique-by-universal-property mediator from Mittens. The concrete instantiations of 'competing cocone' in the section's discourse — never bare 'Y'." ;
    silm:groundsIn cco:ont00000958 .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_decomposition_step__step_nathoma_____f%5Eco
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Nat names the set of natural transformations between two functors. Hom(A, -) names the COVARIANT representable functor at A: for each downstream object Y, Hom(A, Y) is the set of arrows from A to Y; this is the OUT-profile. F^{co} names a covariant functor D_Mittens -> Set (in contrast to the contravariant presheaves of section 06)." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_decomposition_step__step_co_yoneda_bijection
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The bijection takes a natural transformation tau in Nat(Hom(MittensColimitApex, -), F^co) and returns the element tau_{MittensColimitApex}(id_{MittensColimitApex}) of F^co(MittensColimitApex). Inversely: take any element x in F^co(MittensColimitApex), and construct the unique natural transformation that sends each arrow f: MittensColimitApex -> Y to F^co(f)(x)." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_decomposition_step__step_co_yoneda_lemma_op_dual_of_yoneda
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The co-Yoneda lemma: for every locally small category C, every object A in C, and every covariant functor F^co: C -> Set, the set Nat(Hom(A, -), F^co) is in bijection with F^co(A). Mac Lane CWM III.2 (stated for the contravariant in-profile; the co-Yoneda is the op-dual, obtained by replacing C with C^{op}). Awodey 8.3." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_decomposition_step__step_mittenscareplanobligations_recovery
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Recovery: the four obligations in MittensCarePlanObligations = {annual_dental_exam_recommended, rabies_boost_q3yr_recommended, feline_specific_vaccine_panel_required, weight_monitoring_q6mo_recommended} are recovered as the four elements of CareplanInheritanceFunctor(MittensColimitApex). Each corresponds bijectively to a natural transformation tau^co: MittensOutProfile -> CareplanInheritanceFunctor. The OUT-profile fully encodes the obligation set." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_decomposition_step__step_spine_inheritance_out_profile__%3E_paper_17_governance
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Paper 17 (Commutative Diagrams as Governance) Yoneda-inherits the out-profile: governance rules are encoded as obligations recovered from the out-arrows of a chartered entity. The co-Yoneda lemma is the formal mechanism: the obligation set on the chartered entity is in bijection with the natural transformations from its out-profile into the obligation functor. Mittens-as-chartered-entity is the worked instance; paper 17 generalises to arbitrary chartered entities." .

silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_07_yoneda_profile_drill_sections_08_co_yoneda_dual_profile_decomposition_step__step_co_yoneda_dual_recap
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Nat(Hom(MittensColimitApex, -), CareplanInheritanceFunctor) iso CareplanInheritanceFunctor(MittensColimitApex): the obligations attached to Mittens are recovered bijectively from the natural transformations out of her out-profile; the OUT-arrows fully encode her downstream content." .

